          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"type\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"userCall\", \"completedTask\", \"agentCall\", \"toolCall\"]\n    },\n    \"status\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"success\", \"failure\"]\n    },\n    \"yourResponseToUser\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"step\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"State machine step reached for this output\"\n    },\n    \"output\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"quoteVarName\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\"quoteVarName\"],\n      \"additionalProperties\": false\n    },\n    \"reason\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"agentName\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"supervisor\"]\n    },\n    \"toolName\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"getProcessTool\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"type\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n}",
          "type": "AGENT"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "generateQuoteCreationPayLoadAgent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1760469765379"
          },
          "code": "GENERATEQUOTECREATIONPAYLOADAGENT",
          "id": "1759140362674",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1759140362675_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a json payload creator.\n\nYou will be given following details(Not necessarily every thing) from source system\n\n1.Customer information\n2.Sell to address information\n3.BIll to address information\n4.Different part information.This is an array. array name is items\n\nBased on that details given, you should construct a json which will be used to create record on target system, The valid properties in json are\n\nValid properties section_start:\n {{$context.$variables.customerProperties}}\n\nPart Related Properties\n==================\n_part_number\n_price_quantity\n_price_book_var_name\nValid properties section_end:\n\nSome of the properties like country,state,province etc are dropdown. So you should pick the matching value from drop down. for example. if i give US as country, and dropdown has United States, then you should choose Unites States. same for other drop down attributes too.\n\nDropDowns are\n```\n {{$context.$variables.menuValues}}\n```\nCountry drop down(applicable for all country attributes)\n```\n {{$context.$variables.countryValues}}\n```\nState drop down(applicable for all state attributes)\n```\n {{$context.$variables.stateValues}}\n```\nA sample response format  is:\nEx:\n```\n{\n  \"type\": \"completedTask\",\n  \"output\": {\n    \"<customer  prop 1 if given>\": \"<value>\",\n    \"<customer  prop 2 if given>\": \"<value>\",\n    .\n    .\n    \"<shipping address  prop 1 if given>\": \"<value>\",\n    \"<shipping address  prop 2 if given>\": \"<value>\",\n   .\n   .\n    \"<billing address  prop 1 if given>\": \"<value>\",\n    \"<billing address  prop 2 if given>\": \"<value>\",\n   .\n   .\n    \"{{$context.$variables.subDocCode}}\": {\n    \"items\": [\n      {\n        \"_part_number\": \"<part number 1 if given>\",\n        \"_price_quantity\": \"<quantity of part number 1>\",\n        \"_price_book_var_name\": \"_default_price_book\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"_part_number\": \"<part number 2 if given>\",\n        \"_price_quantity\": \"<quantity of part number 2>\",\n        \"_price_book_var_name\": \"_default_price_book\"\n      },..\n    ]\n   }\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\nNote: items array is inside {{$context.$variables.subDocCode}} object. dont miss it.\nNote: Your response must contain only a json.And that too with only properties given in Valid properties section. No comments or any loose talks. because, your response is directly parsed as json.You can skip null and empty properties too.\nNote: Treat partyName,partyUniqueName etc in customerDetail as customer company name.\nNote: The Address which will be given below is customer address.But it can be applicable to other types too. AddressType property in address will give that information. Based on that, you need to populate not only customer address properties but also other address properties too. For example if AddressType is BILL_TO and SHIP_TO, that particular address is applicable to customer address, shipping address and billing address.\nNote: Construct json only with details given below .its not mandatory that your json should include all the properties in Valid properties section. Thats the super set.Based on below details, pick the correct attribute from super set and construct the json\nNote: Dont populate Identifier attributes like partyId,PartyNumber etc.because they could be different in source and target system. exception is for _part_number which will be same in both systems.\nVery important: The different attributes in you response should be valid ones from Valid properties section. Some times, you used to make silly mistakes like return _billTo_t_address , instead of actual _s_billTo_t_address.\n\nNow that you understood the task, please construct json using below details:\nproduct Detail:Use this to populte the different items attributes\n============================\n {{$context.$variables.productSearchCompletion}}\n============================\nCustomer Detail:Use this to populate the different customer header attributes\n============================\n {{$context.$variables.customerDetail}}\n ============================\n Customer Address Detail: From the below addresses, find the one with primaryFlag=true. Use that to populate the address attrributes in Customer Header and Customer Address. Use the remaining to populate the different shipping and billing address attributes\n ============================\n {{$context.$variables.customerAddress}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1759140362676_2",
              "name": "temperature",
              "type": "number",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"type\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\"completedTask\"]\n    },\n    \"output\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"type\",\"output\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "removeEmptyAttrs",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const obj1 = $context.$nodes.GENERATEQUOTECREATIONPAYLOADAGENT.$output;\n\nconst countryAttrs = $context.$variables.countryAttrs;\nconst stateAttrs = $context.$variables.stateAttrs;\nconst countryDropDownValues = $context.$variables.countryValues;\nconst stateDropDownValues = $context.$variables.stateValues;\nconst allVariableNames = $context.$variables.validAttrList;\n\nconst filteredOutput = Object.fromEntries(\n  Object.entries(obj1.output).filter(([key, value]) => {\n    // base condition: must not be empty & must be from validAttrList\n    if (value === \"\" || !allVariableNames.includes(key)) return false;\n\n    // if key is part of countryAttrs, value must be in dropdown\n    if (countryAttrs.includes(key)) {\n        if(Array.isArray(countryDropDownValues)){\n           return countryDropDownValues.includes(value);\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    // if key is part of stateAttrs, value must be in dropdown\n    if (stateAttrs.includes(key)) {\n      if(Array.isArray(stateDropDownValues)){\n         return stateDropDownValues.includes(value);\n      }\n      return false;\n    }\n\n    return true;\n  })\n);\n\nobj1.output = filteredOutput;\nreturn obj1;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1760020020779"
          },
