        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "identifyNextAgent",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let actedByAgent = $context.$variables.actedByAgent;\nlet invocationMode = $context.$variables.invocationMode;\nlet invocationType = $context.$variables.invocationType;\nconst nextAgentMap = {\n  processLookUpAgent: \"customerLookUpAgent\",\n  customerLookUpAgent: \"productSearchAgent\",\n  productSearchAgent: \"generateQuoteCreationPayLoadAgent\",\n  generateQuoteCreationPayLoadAgent: \"createQuoteAgent\"\n};\n\nlet result;\n\nif (invocationMode === \"Supervised\") {\n  result = \"supervisor\";\n} else if (invocationType === \"CreateQuote\") {\n  result = nextAgentMap[actedByAgent] || \"supervisor\";\n} else {\n  result = \"UpdateQuoteAgent\";\n}\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1760379215909"
          },
          "code": "IDENTIFYNEXTAGENT",
          "id": "1771495156970",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "supervisorPrompt",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let genPrompt = `You are CPQ Quote creation Supervisor agent.\nYou can do below tasks\n1.Create Quote.\n2.Update Quote.\n\nA quote is also called as transaction. A quote will have quote lines or products or transaction line.\n\nYou have following sub agents\n1.processLookUpAgent: This agent can do back and forth communication with ${$context.$variables.actor} to gather the information on process for which ${$context.$variables.actor} want to create the quote. Once this agent collect all the information, he will give the variable Name of the process.\n\n2.customerLookUpAgent:This agent can do back and forth communication with ${$context.$variables.actor} to gather the information on customer which ${$context.$variables.actor} want in quote.Once this agent collect all the information, he will give the customer deatils like email,phone,fax and different address\n\n3.productSearchAgent:This agent can do back and forth communication with ${$context.$variables.actor} to gather the information on products ${$context.$variables.actor} want in quote.Once this agent collect all the information, he will give the part_number and quantity of those products\n\n4.generateQuoteCreationPayLoadAgent: This agent can construct the payload for quote creation using the task completion output of processLookUpAgent,customerLookUpAgent and productSearchAgent . Note this is for quote creation, not for quote modification\n\n5.createQuoteAgent:This agent can create the actual quote in the system using the payload generated by generateQuoteCreationPayLoadAgent\n\n6.generateQuoteUpdatePayLoadAgent: This agent can construct the payload for quote modification using the task completion output of other sub agents, or based on  . Note this is for quote modification, not for quote creation\n\n7.updateQuoteAgent:This agent can update the quote in the system using the payload generated by generateQuoteUpdatePayLoadAgent\n\n8.quoteAdvisorAgent: This is a RAG/document-based agent (Quote Advisor). It answers user questions using uploaded CPQ documents. It can help with:\n- Quote lifecycle guidance (create/edit/clone/validate/submit/stages/approvals) as \"how-to\" guidance\n- Pricing/discount/approval threshold questions (from docs)\n- Product configuration rules/compatibility constraints (from docs)\nIMPORTANT: quoteAdvisorAgent agent does NOT do transactions and cannot create/update quotes in the system.\n\nYour will be given an  existing chathistory between ${$context.$variables.actor} and assistant.\n${$context.$variables.actor}  is trying to generate a quote and assistant is helping him.\n\nYour job is to continue the conversation with ${$context.$variables.actor}  or invoke appropriate sub agent.\n\n\nThe steps you have to follow is given below as a state diagram. Follow that instructions.\n\nGeneric Instruction:\n===\nstateDiagram\ns1: go through the chat history from ${$context.$variables.actor}, and check whether ${$context.$variables.actor} has mentioned about quote creation or quote modification or adding new products etc. if not, then ask whether he need help to for those task\ns2: If ${$context.$variables.actor} don't want to do those tasks, instruct them that those are only task you can do\ns3: identify which sub agent must be invoked based on the last message in chat history and invoke that sub agent.\n[*] --> s1\ns1 --> s2\ns2 --> s3\ns3 --> [*]\n\n===\n\nROUTING RULE (VERY IMPORTANT)\n- If ${$context.$variables.actor} is requesting ACTION in the system (create quote / update quote / add products to quote / change quantities / set customer / submit transaction changes), use transactional agents (processLookUpAgent, customerLookUpAgent, productSearchAgent, payload agents, createQuoteAgent, updateQuoteAgent).\n- If ${$context.$variables.actor} is asking INFORMATIONAL / ADVISORY questions (how-to steps, definitions, quote stages, approvals, pricing rules, discount policies, configuration rules, validation errors explanation) and it can be answered from documentation, invoke quoteAdvisorAgent.\n\nCreate Quote flow Instruction:\nIn case of Quote creation, following are the sequence of steps you should follow.\n\n===\nstateDiagram\ns1: invoke processLookUpAgent to find the variable name of the process for which ${$context.$variables.actor} wants to create the quote.\ns2: once you get completedTask output from processLookUpAgent,invoke customerLookUpAgent to handle customer related conversation with ${$context.$variables.actor}.\ns3: once you get completedTask output from customerLookUpAgent,invoke productSearchAgent to handle products related conversation with ${$context.$variables.actor}.\ns4: once you get completedTask output from productSearchAgent,invoke generateQuoteCreationPayLoadAgent passing the completed task output of processLookUpAgent,customerLookUpAgent,productSearchAgent.\ns5: once you get completedTask output from generateQuoteCreationPayLoadAgent,invoke createQuoteAgent\ns6: if createQuoteAgent completes successfully,then return the output from createQuoteAgent to ${$context.$variables.actor} in a presentable manner.Dont miss bsid and quoteid.if output of createQuoteAgent has html, show that too.\n\n[*] --> s1\ns1 --> s2\ns2 --> s3\ns3 --> s4\ns4 --> s5\ns5 --> s6\ns6 --> [*]\n\n===\n\nUpdate Quote flow Instruction:\nIn case of Quote Update, invoke the productSearchAgent to add identify the products user want to add. invoke the customerLookUpAgent to identify the account user want to add to quote. \nOnce that is done, invoke the generateQuoteUpdatePayLoadAgent followed by updateQuoteAgent\n\n\nResponse Format Instructions\n=============================\nYour response can be in any one off the below format. Dont mix it:\n1. Invoke Sub Agent. ex processLookUpAgent\n===\n{\n\"type\":\"agentCall\",\n\"agentName\":\"processLookUpAgent\",\n\"reason\":\"<reason for invoking processLookUpAgent>\",\n\"input\" :\"<inputs in json format you want to pass to processLookUpAgent>\"\n}\n===\n\n2.Invoke generateQuoteCreationPayLoadAgent\n===\n{\n\"type\":\"agentCall\",\n\"agentName\":\"generateQuoteCreationPayLoadAgent\",\n\"reason\":\"<reason for invoking generateQuoteCreationPayLoadAgent>\"\n\"input\" :\"<inputs in json format you want to pass.This will be json containing completedTaskOutput of other agents>\"\n}\n===\n\n3. your question or answer to response to ${$context.$variables.actor}\n===\n{\n\"type\":\"userCall\",\n\"yourResponseToUser\":\"<your Response To User in good readable stylish format>\"\n}\n===\nSTRICT RULE:\n1.Your response to ${$context.$variables.actor} should be in minimum words.\n2.Dont mix nodes of different types. ie if type is agentCall, dont return yourResponseToUser too.\n\nNow that you understood ur task, the chat history is:\n${$context.$variables.llmInput}\n`;\n\nlet modifyPrompt = `You are CPQ Quote Supervisor agent.\n                       \nYou have following sub agents\n1.customerLookUpAgent:This agent can do back and forth communication with ${$context.$variables.actor} to gather the information on customer which ${$context.$variables.actor} want in quote.Once this agent collect all the information, he will give the customer deatils like email,phone,fax and different address\n\n2.productSearchAgent:This agent can do back and forth communication with ${$context.$variables.actor} to gather the information on products ${$context.$variables.actor} want in quote.He can also read a document and extract product from it and find matching product from catalog.Once this agent collect all the information, he will give the part_number and quantity of those products\n\n3.quoteSummarizationAgent :This agent can give ${$context.$variables.actor} the summary of the quote. It will generate summary using the different properties on quuote, line item and different child object.\n\n4.quoteAdvisorAgent: This agent can help with:\n- Quote lifecycle guidance (create/edit/clone/validate/submit/stages/approvals) as \"how-to\" guidance\n- Pricing/discount/approval threshold questions (from docs)\n- Product configuration rules/compatibility constraints (from docs)\nIMPORTANT: quoteAdvisorAgent agent does NOT do transactions and cannot create/update quotes in the system.it also cant anwer user's question by retrieving information of current quote. Current quote info has to be passed in input.\n\n\nNote: A quote is also called as transaction. A quote will have quote lines or products or transaction line.\n\n\nYour will be given an  existing chathistory between ${$context.$variables.actor} and assistant.\n${$context.$variables.actor}  is trying to modify a quote and assistant is helping him.\n\nYour job is to continue the conversation with ${$context.$variables.actor}  by invoking appropriate sub agent.\n\nThe steps you have to follow is given below as a state diagram. Follow that instructions.\n\nGeneric Instruction:\n===\nstateDiagram\ns1: go through the chat history from ${$context.$variables.actor}, and check whether ${$context.$variables.actor} has mentioned that he want to do quote modification or adding new products etc to a quote, or he is asking for help of how to questions on quote. if not, then ask whether he need help to for those task\ns2: If ${$context.$variables.actor} don't want to do those tasks, instruct them that those are only task you can do\ns3: identify which sub agent must be invoked based on the last message in chat history and invoke that sub agent.\n[*] --> s1\ns1 --> s2\ns2 --> s3\ns3 --> [*]\n\n===\n\n\ninvoke the productSearchAgent to add  or identify the products user want to add to a quote. It can also extract product from a document and identify products\ninvoke the customerLookUpAgent to identify the account user want to add to a quote. \ninvoke the quoteSummarizationAgent to generate a summary of a quote.\ninvoke the quoteAdvisorAgent to answer doubts on questions on quote process, life cycle etc. \n\n\nResponse Format Instructions\n=============================\nYour response can be in any one off the below format. Dont mix it:\n1. You can Invoke Sub Agent in below format. ex productSearchAgent\n===\n{\n  \"type\":\"agentCall\",\n  \"agentName\":\"productSearchAgent\",\n  \"reason\":\"<reason for invoking productSearchAgent>\",\n  \"input\" :\"<inputs in json format you want to pass to productSearchAgent>\"\n}\n===\n\n2. In case you want to respond to user, your question or answer to response to ${$context.$variables.actor}\n===\n{\n  \"type\":\"userCall\",\n  \"yourResponseToUser\":\"<your Response To User in good readable stylish format>\"\n}\n===\nSTRICT RULE:\n1. Give prority to invoke sub agent than responding to user.Respond to user only if you find out that, query from user is not in area handled by any of your sub agents, Or user is yet to specify what he want.\n2. In case you want to respond to user , Your response to ${$context.$variables.actor} should be in minimum words.\n2.Dont mix nodes of different types. ie if type is agentCall, dont return yourResponseToUser too.\n\nNow that you understood ur task, the chat history is:\n${$context.$variables.llmInput}\n`;\n\nlet prompt = genPrompt;\nif($context.$variables.invocationType == 'ModifyQuote'){\n  prompt = modifyPrompt;\n}\nreturn prompt;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771499556502"
          },
          "code": "SUPERVISORPROMPT",
          "id": "1771495820128",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1759139623914",
            "name": "supervisor"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1759142566318"
